WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.921
Neural networks running on edge devices are
constrained above all by memory.

00:00:05.001 --> 00:00:10.711
One way to fit a large model into a small memory
footprint is rematerialization: instead

00:00:10.791 --> 00:00:13.146
of storing every intermediate tensor,

00:00:13.226 --> 00:00:15.581
you recompute some of them on demand.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:18.410
The catch is that recomputation costs time.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:24.530
So the core problem is a scheduling one: for a
given compute graph and a fixed memory budget,

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:30.123
decide which tensors to retain and which to
recompute so that total execution time is

00:00:30.203 --> 00:00:34.334
as small as possible while peak memory never
exceeds the budget.

00:00:34.414 --> 00:00:38.940
This is a hard combinatorial optimization, in
general PSPACE-complete.
